> =A0lo selma'o be zo la'e

That's what I say!

Also, you can drop a syllable if you elide the relationship between zo
la'e and the selma'o:

   "lo zo la'e selma'o"

And also, since the word "la'e" is used as a symbol for the selma'o,
it makes sense to me to just say:

   "la'e zo la'e"

As in:

   "zo la'e cmavo la'e zo la'e"

mi'e la stela selckiku
